{"name":"Parlour Red","hex":"#a12d5d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"parlour","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of parlor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parlour"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Parlour","blocks":[{"text":"A parlour is a reception room or public space. In medieval Christian Europe, the \"outer parlour\" was the room where the monks or nuns conducted business with those outside the monastery and the \"inner parlour\" was used for necessary conversation between resident members. In the English-speaking world of the 18th and 19th century, having a parlour room was evidence of social status."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Ca%27_Rezzonico_-_Il_Parlatorio_delle_monache_di_San_Zaccaria_-_Francesco_Guardi.jpg/330px-Ca%27_Rezzonico_-_Il_Parlatorio_delle_monache_di_San_Zaccaria_-_Francesco_Guardi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parlour","wikidata":"Q10550521"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Photograph_of_a_Greek_Revival_Parlor_in_the_Metropolitan.jpg/500px-Photograph_of_a_Greek_Revival_Parlor_in_the_Metropolitan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Photograph_of_a_Greek_Revival_Parlor_in_the_Metropolitan.jpg/1280px-Photograph_of_a_Greek_Revival_Parlor_in_the_Metropolitan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Photograph_of_a_Greek_Revival_Parlor_in_the_Metropolitan.jpg/500px-Photograph_of_a_Greek_Revival_Parlor_in_the_Metropolitan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Greek Revival parlour in the Metropolitan Museum of Art","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APhotograph_of_a_Greek_Revival_Parlor_in_the_Metropolitan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Georg_Janny_Salon_im_Makartstil.jpg/500px-Georg_Janny_Salon_im_Makartstil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Georg_Janny_Salon_im_Makartstil.jpg/1280px-Georg_Janny_Salon_im_Makartstil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Georg_Janny_Salon_im_Makartstil.jpg/500px-Georg_Janny_Salon_im_Makartstil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_ca